<title>SWITZERLAND: Novartis CEO sees higher 1997 profit.</title>
<headline>Novartis CEO sees higher 1997 profit.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Designated chief executive Daniel Vasella said he expected Novartis AG, formed from the merger of Ciba-Geigy AG and Sandoz AG, to show continuing profit growth in 1997.  </p>
<p>Profits will be boosted at least by the amount of costs saved due to synergies from the merger of Sandoz and Ciba, Vasella told Reuters after a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the simple logical consequence (of cost savings). If you at it, you know what will be cut and there should therefore be some growth,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
